    "narrative": "Today\u2019s lineup centers on capitalizing on the vulnerability of Zac Gallen, who serves as a catalyst for our high-upside plays. **Taylor Ward** leads our daily efficiency board with a 71.18 score, benefiting from a soft matchup against Schultz and a significant park factor boost. Our strongest core plays against Gallen are **Luis Arraez** (69.53), **Matt Chapman** (68.53), and **Jung Hoo Lee** (68.02). These three aren't just benefiting from a favorable xERA; the projected \"slow delivery\" timing from the mound provides a clear window for our speed-oriented strategy, adding a vital 2% boost to their floor as we hunt for stolen bases in a thin market. **Daulton Varsho** (65.07) and **Jonathan Aranda** (68.94) also project as elite starts, with **Jonathan Aranda** specifically benefiting from a wind-out scenario that elevates his power profile against Lugo.\n\nThe most difficult bench decision involved **Tyler Freeman**, who posted a 56.25 score. He was squeezed out by the efficiency of **Geraldo Perdomo** (57.75) and the necessity of keeping **Masyn Winn** (59.48) in the middle infield. While **Tyler Freeman** thrives in high-park-factor environments, the optimizer prioritized the higher base projections and platoon reliability of our starters. We are keeping a close eye on the lineup cards for **Luis Arraez**, **Geraldo Perdomo**, **Matt Chapman**, **Drew Gilbert**, **Lawrence Butler**, and **Jung Hoo Lee**. With six players officially listed as \"Lineup Pending,\" our projected scores\u2014particularly for **Drew Gilbert** (58.86) and **Lawrence Butler** (60.79)\u2014are subject to volatility; if any of these pieces drop lower in their respective batting orders, we may see a reshuffle to protect our daily game caps. **Bryson Stott** remains on the bench, as his matchup against the elite Skenes creates too much risk compared to the favorable environment our active starters are facing today.",
